content.text:
{
  "company": "CRONUS International Ltd.",
  "messageType": "Inventory.ItemCharge.Assign",
  "status": "Success",
  "contract": "json",
  "format": "chapters",
  "catalogue": {
    "name": "Inventory.ItemCharge.Assign",
    "isEnabled": true,
    "filterTableNo": 5805,
    "description": "Assigns a purchase or sales item charge to item lines, receipts or shipments.",
    "selectionDescription": "Spreads freight, customs or another item charge over item lines equally, by amount, by weight or by volume, so the cost lands on the items.",
    "messageDirection": "Inbound",
    "keywords": [
      "item charge",
      "assign",
      "freight",
      "customs",
      "landed cost"
    ],
    "chargeable": true
  },
  "chapters": {
    "envelope": {
      "subject": {
        "use": "notUsed",
        "description": "The charge line is named under data.documentType, data.documentNo or data.systemId, and data.lineNo; subject is not read."
      },
      "dataRequired": true,
      "version": "1.0",
      "contentType": "text/json"
    },
    "target": [
      {
        "source": "data.documentNo",
        "form": "document no.",
        "description": "The No. of the open purchase or sales document that holds the charge line. data.documentType says which kind of document it is."
      },
      {
        "source": "data.systemId",
        "form": "guid",
        "description": "The system id of that document, as an alternative to data.documentNo. Send one of them, not both."
      },
      {
        "source": "data.lineNo",
        "form": "integer",
        "description": "The charge line, named by its document and line number."
      }
    ],
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "documentType",
        "type": "string",
        "required": true,
        "description": "purchase or sales. Says which kind of document holds the charge line."
      },
      {
        "name": "documentNo",
        "type": "string",
        "required": false,
        "description": "Number of the open purchase or sales document (order, invoice, return order or credit memo). Send this or systemId."
      },
      {
        "name": "systemId",
        "type": "string",
        "required": false,
        "description": "systemId of the document. Send this or documentNo."
      },
      {
        "name": "lineNo",
        "type": "integer",
        "required": true,
        "description": "Line number of the Charge (Item) line."
      },
      {
        "name": "method",
        "type": "string",
        "required": false,
        "description": "equally, byAmount, byWeight or byVolume. Spreads the charge over the item lines of the same document, as Suggest Item Charge Assignment does. Send this or targets."
      },
      {
        "name": "targets",
        "type": "array",
        "required": false,
        "description": "Explicit lines to assign to. Each entry has appliesToDocType, documentNo, lineNo and qtyToAssign. appliesToDocType is order, invoice, returnOrder or creditMemo for an open document line, or receipt, transferReceipt, returnShipment, salesShipment or returnReceipt (purchase) and shipment or returnReceipt (sales) for a posted line. Send this or method.",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "appliesToDocType",
            "type": "string",
            "required": true,
            "description": "What the target line is: order, invoice, returnOrder or creditMemo for an open document line, or a posted line type (see targets)."
          },
          {
            "name": "documentNo",
            "type": "string",
            "required": true,
            "description": "No. of the document the target line belongs to."
          },
          {
            "name": "lineNo",
            "type": "integer",
            "required": true,
            "description": "Line number of the target line on that document."
          },
          {
            "name": "qtyToAssign",
            "type": "number",
            "required": true,
            "description": "Quantity of the charge to assign to that line. It must be greater than zero."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "response": {
      "contentType": "text/json",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "status",
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Success on a successful call; Error responses use the standard error envelope."
        },
        {
          "name": "documentType",
          "type": "string",
          "description": "purchase or sales, in lower case."
        },
        {
          "name": "documentNo",
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The No. of the document that holds the charge line."
        },
        {
          "name": "lineNo",
          "type": "integer",
          "description": "The line number of the charge line."
        },
        {
          "name": "replacedCount",
          "type": "integer",
          "description": "The number of assignment rows the charge line had before the call. Rows without an invoiced quantity are deleted; rows that are already partly invoiced are kept with qtyToAssign set to zero."
        },
        {
          "name": "assignments",
          "type": "array",
          "description": "The assignment rows of the charge line, in row order.",
          "children": [
            {
              "name": "lineNo",
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "The line number of the assignment row."
            },
            {
              "name": "appliesToDocType",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "What the charge lands on: order, invoice, returnOrder, creditMemo, receipt, transferReceipt, returnShipment, salesShipment, shipment, returnReceipt, quote or blanketOrder."
            },
            {
              "name": "appliesToDocNo",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The No. of the document the charge lands on."
            },
            {
              "name": "appliesToDocLineNo",
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "The line number on that document."
            },
            {
              "name": "itemNo",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The item the charge lands on."
            },
            {
              "name": "description",
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The description of the assignment row."
            },
            {
              "name": "qtyToAssign",
              "type": "decimal",
              "description": "The quantity of the charge assigned to that line and not yet invoiced."
            },
            {
              "name": "amountToAssign",
              "type": "decimal",
              "description": "The amount of the charge assigned to that line and not yet invoiced."
            },
            {
              "name": "qtyAssigned",
              "type": "decimal",
              "description": "The quantity of the charge that is already invoiced."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "errors": [
      {
        "code": "MissingParameter",
        "when": "documentType or lineNo is missing, neither documentNo nor systemId was sent, neither method nor targets was sent, or a target lacks a key.",
        "fix": "Send documentType, lineNo, documentNo or systemId, and method or targets."
      },
      {
        "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
        "when": "A key has the wrong JSON type, systemId is not a GUID, or a target is not an object.",
        "fix": "Send documentType, documentNo, systemId and method as text, lineNo as a whole number, and targets as an array of objects."
      },
      {
        "code": "UnknownParameter",
        "when": "The request or a target contains a key this type does not read.",
        "fix": "Remove the unknown key. Allowed keys are documentType, documentNo, systemId, lineNo, method and targets; a target allows appliesToDocType, documentNo, lineNo and qtyToAssign."
      },
      {
        "code": "RecordNotFound",
        "when": "No open document, no charge line or no target line matched.",
        "fix": "Check documentNo or systemId, documentType and lineNo, and the documentNo and lineNo of each target."
      },
      {
        "code": "AmbiguousRecord",
        "when": "Several documents of different types have this number.",
        "fix": "Send the systemId of the document instead of documentNo."
      },
      {
        "code": "ConflictingIdentifiers",
        "when": "documentNo and systemId were both sent, or method and targets were both sent.",
        "fix": "Send one of documentNo or systemId, and one of method or targets."
      },
      {
        "code": "PreconditionFailed",
        "when": "The line is not an item charge line.",
        "fix": "Pass the line no. of a Charge (Item) line."
      },
      {
        "code": "PreconditionFailed",
        "when": "The charge line has no quantity to invoice, or the document has no item line to spread the charge over.",
        "fix": "Set a quantity to invoice on the charge line, add an item line, or send targets with posted lines."
      },
      {
        "code": "InvalidLine",
        "when": "A target line is not an item line or belongs to another vendor or customer.",
        "fix": "Use lines from the same vendor/customer."
      },
      {
        "code": "InvalidParameter",
        "when": "byWeight or byVolume was requested and the item lines have no weight or volume.",
        "fix": "Use equally or byAmount, or fill the item's weight/volume."
      },
      {
        "code": "InvalidParameter",
        "when": "documentType, method or appliesToDocType has a value this type does not know, or qtyToAssign is not greater than zero.",
        "fix": "Send purchase or sales, one of the listed methods and target types, and a positive qtyToAssign."
      },
      {
        "code": "PermissionDenied",
        "when": "The caller cannot change item charge assignments or read the document.",
        "fix": "Assign the Bifrost \"Full Access\" permission set (extended by Inventory write permissions) and a Business Central permission set that can change these tables."
      },
      {
        "code": "BusinessCentralError",
        "when": "Business Central refused the assignment, for example because the charge line is already fully invoiced.",
        "fix": "Read the error text, correct the document in Business Central, and send the request again."
      },
      {
        "code": "InvalidParameter",
        "when": "The Item Charge domain is turned off for this company.",
        "fix": "Turn the domain on from the Inventory Setup page, then send the call again."
      }
    ],
    "effect": {
      "effect": "write",
      "writes": true,
      "posts": false,
      "changes": "Replaces the item charge assignment of the charge line: rows without an invoiced quantity are deleted, rows that are already partly invoiced are kept with qtyToAssign set to zero, and the new rows are inserted. The document is not posted. A refusal saves nothing. Chained Omit Commit calls stay in the caller transaction; standalone calls use an isolated write.",
      "idempotent": true,
      "permissionSet": "the Bifrost \"Full Access\" permission set",
      "preconditions": [
        "The document is an open order, invoice, return order or credit memo, and lineNo is a Charge (Item) line on it.",
        "The charge line has a quantity to invoice."
      ]
    },
    "metering": {
      "chargeable": true,
      "chargedAs": "message"
    },
    "related": [
      {
        "name": "Inventory.ItemCharge.Get",
        "useInsteadWhen": "Read the current assignment and the unassigned quantity without changing anything."
      },
      {
        "name": "Purchase.Document.Post",
        "useInsteadWhen": "Post the purchase document once the charge is assigned; this type does not post."
      },
      {
        "name": "Sales.Document.Post",
        "useInsteadWhen": "Post the sales document once the charge is assigned; this type does not post."
      }
    ],
    "workflow": {
      "steps": [
        {
          "messageType": "Inventory.ItemCharge.Get",
          "purpose": "Read the current assignment and the quantity that is still unassigned."
        },
        {
          "messageType": "Inventory.ItemCharge.Assign",
          "purpose": "Spread the charge over the item lines with method, or over named lines with targets."
        },
        {
          "messageType": "Purchase.Document.Post",
          "purpose": "Post the purchase document so the assigned charge lands on the items."
        },
        {
          "messageType": "Sales.Document.Post",
          "purpose": "Post the sales document so the assigned charge lands on the items."
        }
      ]
    },
    "examples": [
      {
        "title": "Spread a freight charge equally over the item lines of a purchase order",
        "request": {
          "type": "Inventory.ItemCharge.Assign",
          "data": {
            "documentType": "purchase",
            "documentNo": "106001",
            "lineNo": 30000,
            "method": "equally"
          }
        },
        "response": {
          "status": "Success",
          "documentType": "purchase",
          "documentNo": "106001",
          "lineNo": 30000,
          "replacedCount": 0,
          "assignments": [
            {
              "lineNo": 10000,
              "appliesToDocType": "order",
              "appliesToDocNo": "106001",
              "appliesToDocLineNo": 10000,
              "itemNo": "1896-S",
              "description": "ATHENS Desk",
              "qtyToAssign": 0.5,
              "amountToAssign": 50,
              "qtyAssigned": 0
            },
            {
              "lineNo": 20000,
              "appliesToDocType": "order",
              "appliesToDocNo": "106001",
              "appliesToDocLineNo": 20000,
              "itemNo": "1900-S",
              "description": "PARIS Guest Chair, black",
              "qtyToAssign": 0.5,
              "amountToAssign": 50,
              "qtyAssigned": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Assign a freight charge on a purchase invoice to a posted receipt line",
        "request": {
          "type": "Inventory.ItemCharge.Assign",
          "data": {
            "documentType": "purchase",
            "documentNo": "108001",
            "lineNo": 10000,
            "targets": [
              {
                "appliesToDocType": "receipt",
                "documentNo": "107001",
                "lineNo": 10000,
                "qtyToAssign": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "response": {
          "status": "Success",
          "documentType": "purchase",
          "documentNo": "108001",
          "lineNo": 10000,
          "replacedCount": 0,
          "assignments": [
            {
              "lineNo": 10000,
              "appliesToDocType": "receipt",
              "appliesToDocNo": "107001",
              "appliesToDocLineNo": 10000,
              "itemNo": "1896-S",
              "description": "ATHENS Desk",
              "qtyToAssign": 1,
              "amountToAssign": 100,
              "qtyAssigned": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "overview": "Assigns a freight, customs or other item charge line on an open purchase or sales document to item lines, so the cost lands on the items, as the Item Charge Assignment page does. Send method to spread the charge over the item lines of the same document (equally, byAmount, byWeight or byVolume), or targets to name the lines yourself, including posted receipt, shipment, transfer receipt and return lines. The answer lists the assignment rows with qtyToAssign and amountToAssign.",
    "notes": "The charge is spread over the quantity to invoice on the charge line. Assigning again replaces the earlier assignment rows of that charge line; replacedCount is the number of rows the charge line had before the call, and rows that are already partly invoiced are not deleted: their quantity to assign is set to zero and they keep their invoiced quantity. A refusal writes nothing. A successful call saves the assignment but does not post the document; post it with the purchase or sales posting message type. Generic record writes to the assignment tables are refused, so use this type to change them. In a chained Omit Commit call, the write remains in the caller transaction and a native failure propagates so the whole chain can roll back."
  },
  "conventions": "## Errors and warnings\r\nAn error response has `status` = `Error`, a stable `code`, the `error` text and, when they apply, `parameter` (the request parameter concerned, e.g. `lines[2].no`), `received` (the value received), `expected` (what was expected) and `nextStep` (what to do now). `hint` says where to read more.\r\nWhen a request has several problems, all of them are listed in `errors[]` - each with the same fields - under a top-level `code` (`MultipleErrors`, or a shared code such as `InvalidLine` for the `lines` of a Create type) and a summary `error`. Fix them all before calling again. One problem is reported at the top level, with no `errors[]`.\r\nRequest values are checked first and every problem found is reported together. A Business Central validation error raised afterwards, while a record is being written, stops the call and is reported on its own: `code` = `BusinessCentralError`, Business Central's own `error` text, and `parameter` naming the request parameter being applied, e.g. `lines[1].accountNo`. Nothing is written.\r\nRequest values are read in one format, whatever the language: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`; date-times ISO 8601 with `Z` or an offset; amounts as JSON numbers (or a string such as `\"1234.56\"`, no thousands separator); integers as JSON integers; booleans `true` or `false`. Any other value is `InvalidParameterFormat` with `received` and `expected`; for an unambiguous local form such as `26.09.2026`, `nextStep` gives the value to resend. Every bad value of a request is reported together.\r\nAnswers are written in one format as well, whatever the language of the call: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`, date-times ISO 8601, numbers with a dot and no thousands separator, and the option and enum values of every answer except `Data.Records.Get` and `Data.Records.Set` as their English names, so a value read from an answer can be sent back. Those two answer the caption of the language of the call, for a person to read. The language of the call (`lcid`) changes captions and message texts, not these forms. Two things are outside Bifrost's control: Business Central writes its own texts (a ledger entry description such as `Direct Cost V00010 on 10/02/26`, the text of a `BusinessCentralError`) with the regional settings of the server session, which `lcid` does not change, so a date in such a text can be in month-day order; and a table view is read with those settings too, so write dates in a view as `YYYY-MM-DD` and decimals with a dot.\r\nBoth success and error responses can carry `warnings[]`, each with `code`, `message` and, when they apply, `parameter` and `nextStep`.\r\n`UnknownParameter` refuses undeclared data keys before execution for every type whose effect is not read, including a missing effect. The root envelope option `strict:false` cannot opt out. Read types keep warnings without changing status, validationResult or domain warningCount unless the caller sets `strict:true` (next to type and subject, never inside data). Refusals list the keys and localized nextStep corrections; no business changes or successful execution charges occur. Example: {\"type\":\"Memory.User.Set\",\"strict\":true,\"data\":{\"memory\":\"test\",\"memry\":\"typo\"}} is refused.\r\n`FieldChangedByBC` is a warning from Data.Records.Set: another field validation or the write changed a sent field after its own validation. `parameter` names data[n].fields.{jsonName}, counting from 0. Status stays Success. Compare the returned values with what you sent; follow `nextStep` to use validation order or send the field again in a separate call. Normalisation of the field itself, LCY, Dimension Set ID, BLOB, Media, MediaSet and skipped fields are excluded.\r\nFeature apps (Foundation 28.0.8 or later) can call `Argument.SetErrorContext(Parameter, Expected, NextStep)` before an operation that may fail after writes, then `Argument.ClearErrorContext()` after success. Supply the parameter name and translated labels, never request values, file content, credentials or a call stack. Foundation returns that context on the original `BusinessCentralError` after rollback, including uncaught task errors; `RespondWithLastError()` also uses it. The API does not catch errors, commit data or change the transaction boundary. Keep no-return `Codeunit.Run` and let errors propagate for chained `OmitCommit` calls; never add a Boolean `Codeunit.Run` or a writing `TryFunction` to recover context. Context is cleared between messages. Existing callers without context keep their response shape; recognized lock errors keep their existing `Retryable` guidance.\r\nA message type that must run only one way (Foundation 28.0.9 or later) reads `Argument.GetInvocationSource()`: `Queue` when the task scheduler runs a message the queue API scheduled, `Task` for the Task API (`/tasks`), `Dispatcher` for an internal call through `Dispatcher ori` (the in-product MCP tool server, a nested dispatch from another message type), `Direct` for the Messages page Run Task action and anything unset. Only Foundation sets it; request values, parameters, source, subject and writes to the argument cannot change it. Refuse the other paths with `PreconditionFailed` and a `nextStep` that names the path to use.\r\n`Retryable` means a transient lock or deadlock caught while writing or posting. `error` keeps Business Central's original text. `expected` is \"no concurrent lock on the same records\"; `nextStep` is \"Retry the same call after a few seconds; nothing was changed.\" Bifrost does not retry automatically. Other platform errors, including uncaught queue-path errors, remain `BusinessCentralError`.\r\nCodes: `MissingParameter`, `InvalidParameterFormat`, `InvalidParameter`, `RecordNotFound`, `AmbiguousRecord`, `ConflictingIdentifiers`, `InvalidFilterField`, `InvalidLine`, `NothingToPreview`, `LinesSkipped`, `BlockedByWriteGuard`, `PreconditionFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `LimitExceeded`, `BusinessCentralError`, `MultipleErrors`, `DeprecatedParameter`, `UnknownParameter`, `FieldChangedByBC`, `Retryable`, `EULA_REQUIRED`, `TRIAL_NOT_STARTED`. The `error` text may be translated; the code never is.\r\n"
}
